< q9
Write `if/elif/else` code that turns a mark into a grade: 75 or more is `"Distinction"`, 50–74 is `"Pass"`, below 50 is `"Fail"`. Test it on `mark = 68`.
< h9
Check the highest band first: `if mark >= 75:` then `elif mark >= 50:`.
< a9
mark = 68
# Python checks top to bottom and stops at the first True condition,
# so the order matters: the highest band goes first
if mark >= 75:
    grade = "Distinction"
elif mark >= 50:
    grade = "Pass"
else:
    grade = "Fail"
print(mark, grade)

